723f6","event_uuid":"f70cb83a-ffbd-487f-a654-cdce0a60aad6","position":{"commit_sha":"8bf5e8381de2ac65f4a5c8cc45271219d247e842","position":"1795244798067049001-f70cb83a-ffbd-487f-a654-cdce0a60aad6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision, 2026-11-20: the simple solution is that CI checks op-cert trust using main's rebar.toml, not the rebar.toml in the change under review. A change can then never widen the trust list of the gate that checks it.","timestamp":1795214879343949001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed as Gerrit 3495, merged d5f10d1d2c8. Root cause: verify-opcert composed config from the repo root, so the change's own rebar.toml was the project layer for require_environment, opcert_enforce_since, trusted_opcert_keys and tracker.dir; plan review also found the read-time sync.pull lookup in ensure_fresh read the working tree. Fix: _opcert_gate_config.gate_config reads the project layer committed on origin/main, the run binds it as the operation snapshot under local_read_context, and verify-identity.yml fetches main first. Checked on merged main: tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py + test_verify_opcert*.py 23 passed; the attack test exits 0 on the pre-fix gate; check_mechanism_delta --check exits 0; _config_schema.py unchanged. make verify green locally (21573 + 226 passed). Not done here: docs/llm-framework.md:1063 still says the trust list never lives in the repository without mentioning the base-branch rule (plan-review advisory); a show_ticket exception still drops a ticket from scope in verify_opcert.cli (pre-existing).","timestamp":1795244217799371001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1795213805057892001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ddce8ef7-cb0a-4170-b233-0eef90f288f5","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90"},{"link_uuid":"4e8941a7-4e06-4f95-81e5-178408635110","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0557-bfa6-4fd8-4c79"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0125 puts `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` in each verifying environment's own configuration, not the repository.\n\nNothing enforces that. `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` is an ordinary `[verify]` key (`src/rebar/_config_schema.py`, `VerifyConfig.trusted_opcert_keys`). The CI op-cert gate is the `verify-opcert` step of `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml`, which runs `rebar verify-opcert` on the checked-out change. `cli()` in `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py` calls `config.compose_config(root=args.root)` and `trusted_opcert_pairs(args.root)` (`src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py:114`), and both resolve the project layer through `_discover_project_config` (`src/rebar/_config_sources.py:160`), which reads the working-tree `rebar.toml`. So a change under review that adds its own key to `rebar.toml`, drops `verify.require_environment`, or sets `[tracker] dir` to an empty directory (the gate also resolves its store through `config.tracker_dir(args.root)`, `verify_opcert.py:131`, and through `show_ticket`/`current_material_fingerprint`) loosens the very gate run that checks it.\n\n## Approach (operator decision, 2026-11-20)\n\nThe gate resolves its trust configuration from main's committed `rebar.toml`, never from the `rebar.toml` in the change under review.\n\nImplement this in-process in `rebar verify-opcert`, so it holds under any CI provider or none:\n\n- New module `src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py` with `gate_config(root) -> (Config, source, OperationSnapshot)`. It composes the `load_config` layers (user, project, env, `-c`), but the project layer is the config committed at the base ref (`git show <ref>:<path>`). Discovery: nearest `rebar.toml`, else `pyproject.toml` with `[tool.rebar]`, from the project root up to the top level. `$REBAR_CONFIG` is ignored (it could name a working-tree file), so `_discover_project_config` is not reused. The working-tree project config is never read.\n- Base ref: `refs/remotes/origin/main` only, the ref attested gates already treat as reviewed main (`rebar.llm.gate_source.DEFAULT_REF`, `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:71`). Failure handling, every arm:\n  - a remote exists but `origin/main` does not resolve: `ConfigError`, exit 2, naming the `git fetch` that fixes it;\n  - `ls-tree` fails, `git show` of a listed path fails (for example a blobless clone cannot fetch the blob), or the TOML does not parse: `ConfigError`, exit 2;\n  - the path is absent at the ref (decided by `git ls-tree --full-tree --name-only <ref> -- <path>`, which reads trees only): fall through to the next candidate, then to an empty project layer;\n  - `git remote` exits non-zero (not a repository, safe.directory refusal): `ConfigError`, exit 2;\n  - no remote at all (`git remote` succeeds and prints nothing): no reviewed branch and no change under review, so the working-tree configuration is kept.\n- `cli()` takes every gate value (`require_environment`, `opcert_enforce_since`, `trusted_opcert_keys`) from the `gate_config` result and calls neither `compose_config` nor `trusted_opcert_pairs(args.root)`; `trusted_opcert_pairs` is split so the gate parses the list it holds (`opcert_pairs(entries)`). It prints the trust source to stderr.\n- The same configuration is returned as an `OperationSnapshot` (`src/rebar/_operation_config.py:81`) and bound for the run with `bind_operation_snapshot`. That covers only snapshot-aware readers — `config.tracker_dir` (`src/rebar/config.py:152`) and `_config_value` — so the store `show_ticket` and the material recomputation walk is main's `tracker.dir`. `load_config`/`compose_config` ignore the snapshot, so two working-tree reads remain in a live `show_ticket` and each is handled:\n  - read-time sync: `ensure_fresh` (`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:230`) calls `_sync_disabled` → `compose_config`, so the change's `sync.pull` would decide whether the store reconverges, and a raising read escapes `show_ticket` and drops the ticket from scope. The gate runs under `local_read_context()` (`reads.py:145`), which returns before that lookup: the gate verifies the store as mounted (the CI step fetches and mounts `tickets` explicitly).\n  - the advisory cross-session warning toggle (`_commands/cross_session.py:46`); `_lib_warn.emit_cross_session_warning` swallows every error and it cannot change the verdict.\n  A test runs the gate in-process from the fixture repo (cwd and `REBAR_ROOT`), defeats the 60 s freshness throttle, and makes every working-tree project-config discovery raise `AssertionError` (not `ConfigError`, which `_sync_disabled` would swallow); it still requires main's `untrusted` verdict. Without `local_read_context()` it fails (0 tickets in scope, exit 0).\n- `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml`: the `verify-opcert` step fetches `refs/heads/main` into `refs/remotes/origin/main` (blobless, after the pack measurement) before running the gate.\n- Docs: the `verify-opcert` parser description (regenerated `src/rebar/_cli/help/*.txt` and `docs/cli-reference.md`), `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/manifest-signing.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md` (the new exit-2 cases), and `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md` (an enforcement flip takes effect after it merges, not in its own gate run).\n\nOut of scope: the environment layer stays (ADR 0125); keeping it, the gate's code and the workflow file out of the change's reach is the CI lane's job. The sibling `verify-identity` gate is not changed.\n\nNo config key, env var or flag is added: the base ref is fixed at `origin/main`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`\n- `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py`\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/verify.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-opcert.txt`, `docs/cli-reference.md`\n- `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml`\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/manifest-signing.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md`, `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\n`tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`, with a local bare repo as `origin`, covers: the end-to-end attack (exit 1 `untrusted` before merge, exit 0 after, and exit 0 on the old gate), an in-process run with working-tree config reads forced to raise, an unfetchable blob in a blobless clone, dirty and committed change configs ignored, `require_environment` not droppable, the environment trust list still applied, `pyproject.toml [tool.rebar]` on main, a redirected `tracker.dir`, a missing `origin/main` (exit 2 naming `git fetch origin`), and a remote-less checkout. The existing remote-less `tests/unit/test_verify_opcert*.py` fixtures pass unchanged. Full `make verify` before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The CI op-cert gate reads `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` from main's committed `rebar.toml`, not the change's: `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml` fetches `origin/main` before `rebar verify-opcert`, and `gate_config` reads the project layer at that ref (`test_gate_config_ignores_the_working_tree_project_config`).\n- [x] A change that adds a key to `rebar.toml` does not widen the trust list its own gate run uses: `test_change_adding_its_own_key_does_not_widen_its_gate_run` passes, and fails against the pre-fix `verify_opcert.py`.\n- [x] The gate run reaches main's verdict with every working-tree project-config read raising: `test_gate_run_never_needs_the_working_tree_project_config` passes.\n- [x] An unfetchable committed `rebar.toml` fails closed: `test_unfetchable_blob_on_main_fails_closed` passes.\n- [x] A change setting `[tracker] dir` cannot redirect the store the gate walks: `test_change_cannot_redirect_the_store_it_walks` passes.\n- [x] No config key, env var or flag is added: `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0 and `git diff origin/main -- src/rebar/_config_schema.py` is empty.\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py tests/unit/test_verify_opcert.py tests/unit/test_verify_opcert_ac_coverage.py` passes.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py","reason":"new: compose and snapshot the gate config with the project layer from origin/main"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py","reason":"use gate_config and bind its snapshot for the run"},{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py","reason":"split opcert_pairs parser out of trusted_opcert_pairs"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/verify.py","reason":"describe where the gate reads its settings"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt","reason":"regenerated help"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-opcert.txt","reason":"regenerated help"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"regenerated reference"},{"path":".github/workflows/verify-identity.yml","reason":"fetch origin/main before verify-opcert"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"document base-branch trust config"},{"path":"docs/manifest-signing.md","reason":"document base-branch trust config"},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"new exit-2 cases"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md","reason":"flip takes effect after it merges"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py","reason":"new: prove a change cannot widen its own gate"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0557-bfa6-4fd8-4c79"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"cee2e2fd-88fa-48fb-a331-efd97e87fd92","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"eca7-e5b5-7640-403f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"A committed rebar.toml can widen the op-cert gate's trust list","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a51b2d0c-f087-4fd3-9f7d-921ccb2f2d68","4ab7cf65-1c1f-446c-aac3-c1be1cc0da11","613a928b-5a4c-45a0-8316-d35557f8fa2c","24adc993-36fe-4b4d-a0ee-70fe0118354b","2cf45433-caef-41db-b656-c92a26628686","4ca26c8b-05d4-4fdf-9dde-b4e8d2a5ff26","d0c282a3-6a3c-4873-9bfe-2a7d02d5d28a","9bbd7d7f-7976-45af-8261-110172d2ede8","710b4815-0216-4951-bf9b-8f8ae31e3440","a301508d-575a-41aa-9441-78e4670c3b29","dd10bb67-401c-4fcb-8ee1-02ebc01e5ca9","14ac51c8-09c8-499d-ae1d-a60215cd46f4","4e8941a7-4e06-4f95-81e5-178408635110","cee2e2fd-88fa-48fb-a331-efd97e87fd92","f70cb83a-ffbd-487f-a654-cdce0a60aad6"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795244798067049002,"uuid":"07273b8c-27fe-4044-ac6b-0ac2a071b381"}